\f1\fs22 Through skinny streets and alleys jagging among tangles of broken buildings bandaged by tired tarpaulins bound loosely with communication cables and power lines, a commando squad of Elvi escorted Tony and Sarah deeper into the heart of the Pale. With scouts ahead and sweepers behind, with four or five others flanking a perimeter, the squad combed the way forward as assiduously as they would comb their hair.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah thought the Elvi were over-reacting, or at least over-acting which, in the aftermath of the gangster-style showdown in the 
\f2\i Memphis Mafia Bar,
\f1\i0  dissolved none of her fear.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony, beholding the exquisite visage of Sarah growing ever more aghast amid she squalor and grime of the Pale, wall-papered the load-bearing walls of his own emotional landscape with a carefree veneer of detachment. With little else to say, he explained, \'91The heart of the Pale swallowed all the roads years ago, only narrow paths and tunnels are left.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91That sounds delightfully urban.\'92 Sarah replied. \'91Where are we going, anyway?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Vegas Show tonight,\'92 one of the flanker-Elvis whispered, as if hunting for wabbits.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony glowed brighter than a Christmas tree. \'91We\'92re going to a Vegas Show?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91
\f2\i The
\f1\i0  Vegas show,\'92 Elmer Elvis corrected. \'91It\'92s our momma\'92s birthday.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah gagged the question rising in her throat: 
\f2\i How do clones know when their momma\'92s birthday is?
\f1\i0  Instead, she asked, \'91PAPER agents want us dead, and we\'92re going to a show?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Safest place in the Ghetto tonight.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I think those creepy wizard dudes are following us,\'92 Tony said.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91They are,\'92 Elmer agreed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91You\'92re not concerned about them?\'92 Sarah asked.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Elmer grunted and grimaced.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91What did they want anyway?\'92 Tony asked, gluing up another layer of, 
\f2\i I\'92m Cool
\f1\i0 .\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91They want to get me pregnant.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The Elvi patrol halted in their tracks and made side-eyes at each other.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91They wanna make you a momma?\'92 Elmer asked solemnly.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah shrugged. \'91I\'92ve had worse propositions.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony stomped about, hoping it would put out his incandescence. \'91You can\'92t be\'97no\'97what the tax? I\'97 you\'97they\'97what?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Steady there, Sir Galahad. I decided years ago I could never be pregnant.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The Elvi shifted on their feet, as if preparing for a fight. \'91Are you not the Holy Momma?\'92 one of them shot at Sarah.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony, seeing his chance to come to Sarah\'92s aid for once, said, \'91Sure, sure, whatever, Holy Momma, Holy Cow, Holy Hand Grenade, whatever you folks want. Just get us to safety. Where are we going again?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Graceland,\'92 Elmer answered.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony was beside himself with glee. \'91We\'92re going to Graceland!\'92\
