\f1\fs22 \'91Chilo, stop rushing ahead,\'92 Kleoboulos chided. \'91They\'92ll catch us following.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The nearer they approached Graceland, the steelier the stares they received from ever denser throngs and clumps of Elvi, and Cloudborne in Elvi garb. Something big was happening; there was festivity in the air, and crowds milled around outside bars and clubs and drank merry.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>For a few seconds, Chilo lost Sarah and Tony in the coagulating crowd. \'91There they go!\'92 he pointed. \'91Down that side alley.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The side alley led to an open market square, where every store-front, tent and flatbed truck displayed the latest in Elvi fashion, which is to say, the same jump suits, leather, cowboy and military outfits they\'92d worn since before their emancipation. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The three sages loitered while Sarah and Tony were led into one of the less ramshackle stores.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Yer going to the Vegas Show?\'92 asked an ageing Elvi, while he picked his teeth and leant against a truck.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Excuse, me?\'92 Solo said.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91The Vegas show, yer know\'97the biggest night of the year round these parts. Seems yer friends are fixing\'92 to go if\'92n they\'92re buying themselves some proper evening wear.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Outfits \'85\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Yeah, outfits. You cain\'92t be going to Graceland looking like asylum escapees. Now yer could join yer friends in that tourist trap over there, but why would yer, if\'92n you can purchase the exact same high-quality merchandise for half the price, from my fine emporium here?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91You mean your truck,\'92 Kleoboulos checked.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Yes\'92n deed.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleoboulos shrugged. From a rack by the truck\'92s tailgate, he selected a jumpsuit of many colours.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91That one comes with a free cape,\'92 the proprietor said.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Oh, I think\'97\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Yer taking the cape,\'92 the proprietor said with increasing aggression, while Solo selected matching leather jacket and pants, and Chilo opted for an army ensemble. \'91To do otherwise would be sacreligious.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleoboulos blinked and capitulated. \'91Where is the dressing room?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Yer standing in it.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91What?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Look around.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleoboulos looked around the market. Everywhere there were Elvi and Cloudborne of all genders stripping and trying on clothes. He took a deep breath, then stripped and dressed. The suit was a near enough fit, so he accepted it rather than undress again in the open. He threw his pyjamas in a nearby oil-drum fire.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Let\'92s take a look at yer,\'92 the proprietor said when the sages had adjusted their garments to their underwhelming satisfaction. \'91Line up!\'92 From a box in the truck passenger footwell, the proprietor produces what looked like three large syringes.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91What are those?\'92 Solo asked.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Epinephrine auto-injectors, in case of anaphylactic	shock.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91None of us \'85\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The proprietor slipped an injector into a pocket on the inside of each of their jackets. The pockets were a perfect, snug fit. \'91They won\'92t let yer in without them. With such a huge crowd in there \'85 if it happens, you\'92ll know.\'92
